  "about": "Every gem the Rails application is installed with: what Bundler resolves for the Gemfile of a generated application (rails 8.1.4, propshaft, sqlite3, puma, importmap-rails, turbo-rails, stimulus-rails, jbuilder, solid_cache, solid_queue, solid_cable, bootsnap, image_processing), with rdoc held at the version Ruby ships so that rbs and its C extension are not needed. Each is installed by prepare.mjs at exactly this version after its age and checksum are checked. Gemfile.lock and variants/minimal/overlay/Gemfile.lock name the same versions (prepare.mjs refuses any other), so Bundler only loads what is installed. A gem with several platform entries is a precompiled one: the entry for the machine is installed. Gems that are part of Ruby itself (fromRuby) are not installed again; the versions are those of Ruby 4.0.1.",
